# NOTE: application.properties is deliberately NOT excluded any more.
# It used to hold literal secrets, so shipping it would have baked the DB
# password, JWT secret and API key into an immutable image layer. It now holds
# only ${PLACEHOLDER} references, so it is safe to ship -- and it has to ship,
# because it is what maps names like GEMINI_API_KEY onto the property Spring
# actually reads (spring.ai.openai.api-key). Without it in the image, that env
# var would be silently ignored and startup would fail.
#
# The real secrets live in the repo-root .env, which is gitignored and is never
# part of this build context (it sits above it), so it cannot leak in.

# Build output - the image builds its own jar in stage 1, and copying a
# host-built target/ in would both bloat the context and risk a stale jar.
target/

# Local tooling / VCS noise - never needed inside the build context.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# Maven wrapper is unused here: the build stage brings its own Maven.
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
